  "statement": "You are given an integer array `nums` of size `n`. For **each** index `i` where `0 <= i < n`, define a subarray `nums[start ... i]` where `start = max(0, i - nums[i])`.\n\nReturn the total sum of all elements from the subarray defined for each index in the array.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** nums = \\[2,3,1\\]\n\n**Output:** 11\n\n**Explanation:**\n\ni\n\nSubarray\n\nSum\n\n0\n\n`nums[0] = [2]`\n\n2\n\n1\n\n`nums[0 ... 1] = [2, 3]`\n\n5\n\n2\n\n`nums[1 ... 2] = [3, 1]`\n\n4\n\n**Total Sum**\n\n \n\n11\n\nThe total sum is 11. Hence, 11 is the output.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** nums = \\[3,1,1,2\\]\n\n**Output:** 13\n\n**Explanation:**\n\ni\n\nSubarray\n\nSum\n\n0\n\n`nums[0] = [3]`\n\n3\n\n1\n\n`nums[0 ... 1] = [3, 1]`\n\n4\n\n2\n\n`nums[1 ... 2] = [1, 1]`\n\n2\n\n3\n\n`nums[1 ... 3] = [1, 1, 2]`\n\n4\n\n**Total Sum**\n\n \n\n13\n\nThe total sum is 13. Hence, 13 is the output.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= n == nums.length <= 100`\n*   `1 <= nums[i] <= 1000`",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= n == nums.length <= 100",
    "1 <= nums[i] <= 1000"
  ],
